      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T14:08:33Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the Ethereum exploit receipt and call trace, QBridgeHandler's verified source and pinned reproduction, handler proxy creation, all four pre-incident Upgraded events, EIP-1967 storage, historical runtime hashes, the corresponding BSC mint, and the complete borrow campaign. The selected transaction calls QBridge 0x20e5e35ba29dc3b540a1aee781d0814d5c77bce6, which calls handler proxy 0x17b7163cf1dbd286e262ddc68b553d899b93f526 and delegates the defective deposit path to QBridgeHandler 0x80d1486ef600cc56d4df9ed33baf53c60d5a629b. Resource 0x00000000000000000000002f422fe9ea622049d6f73f81a906b9b8cff03b7f01 resolved to address zero. The handler's low-level transferFrom therefore moved no token but returned success and allowed a Deposit event for 3,184 ETH at nonce 92; BSC transaction 0x38692d17fdc9c3da9c1cb234108d78011b086235ce5da2220675a2cf05393cc8 minted the corresponding unbacked qXETH. Across the same campaign, 16 zero-value Ethereum deposits enabled 20 successful borrow transactions from blocks 14742004 through 14742368. Every successful call emitted a same-amount Borrow event; the reverted transaction 0xe9ebf039d630212e55667cf52c3014356982efc0e163a637677829940fc6526b is excluded. Successful borrow hashes: 0x4d2112f716d6a8c2661d7a7f8028f5426a63894e9281151b60818aedfecd7c31, 0xcfa4379af6fb1da547ae7270485b63f304b1fbec55f2a0c1ccf0a4f59d839b2e, 0xa39e732332604f70180ae8107b1a9315e8f7cc7f6108f3235bdb46867b40bd7a, 0xeed6cb886729d654cbb192d9e5a749f6e176ced130cbaecb5a656ac4164259db, 0x4c32d6b8da9be2471a52b921c198b4188f784f12f46557a06753eecd8340aa47, 0x103d3be5194a9ba62a9539532511c9a16e320580726a113476ae589c0ed0e452, 0x4d13ebfed4694de569dd64516306090d26193442c0807fb5c937158653dfc0d0, 0x0294daab79affea4a829be01bae1f6d4216c3124e90b54fd23c5bb8a124002d9, 0xc55995dbb50194b216070cd404f13470b12cf3ea424ab5e93c6d0bd8c8b0fb3d, 0x1786147bc75cbc839637d851ea610caefd41c610c6bcb07f9b0c598047208462, 0xca572ac9a35d33fd52c8146976e680ad0ca2329d77a922c68ad8771de6af3128, 0x405dde